  "body": "The list of available images _does not_ allow coalescing in-flight image requests. This is because we do not add an image to this list [until the image is finished downloading and the `load` event is about to be fired](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#:~:text=completely%20available%20state.-,Add%20the%20image%20to%20the%20list%20of%20available%20images%20using%20the%20key,-key%2C%20with%20the). This is also explicitly stated as a goal in the spec [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#:~:text=It%20is%20not%20used%20to%20avoid%20re-downloading%20the%20same%20image%20while%20the%20previous%20image%20is%20still%20loading.).\r\n\r\nGiven this, I'm wondering why disallowing in-flight request coalescing is an explicit goal of the spec? It seems that all implementations allow this, as I discovered in crrev.com/c/3133524 where I add a a test for this that all implementations fail. In order to change this, I suppose we would just add to the list right before we Fetch. We'd be adding an incomplete image to the list but it would allow multiple `<img>`s to share the same pending request, which seems useful.",
